{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently underestimates the speed of price recovery following sharp drops (e.g., Jan 2023 and May 2023), failing to capture the V-shaped rebound where prices surged 15-20% above the forecast within 10-15 days.",
    "Adjust for sentiment-ignored volatility: Positive sentiment spikes (0.20-0.40) in the history do not trigger upward forecast adjustments; the model remains anchored to a slow, linear drift, missing the subsequent momentum-driven rallies.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot on peaks: The model's linear upward trajectory causes it to overestimate prices during the initial phase of a rally (first 5-7 days) before the true market corrects downward, indicating a need for a non-linear dampening factor on the forecast slope.",
    "Incorporate volatility clustering: The model fails to predict the high-frequency oscillations (choppy markets) seen in the true outcomes, smoothing them into a monotonic trend; forecasts should be widened to include a volatility band rather than a single deterministic path."
  ]
}
